overflowed its stack

Blocker: chelis#2307 -- Std.Io.Json parses with depth proportional to the
element count, so load_json exhausts the evaluator stack before Coral sees the
document. Measured at the 0.19.1 pin: load_json alone, with no Coral symbol on
the path, passes at 960 elements and overflows at 975, for both an array of
objects and an array of bare scalars. read_json_frame's own ceiling (954 pass /
993 fail) is that bound and nothing of Coral's.

Fixed upstream by chelis#3336, merged after v0.19.1 and therefore not in the
pinned toolchain. De-narrowing: when this probe reports FIX-detected at a pin
bump, promote it to tests/io.ch, raise the row count to match the CSV paths,
and archive the docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md entry.
